---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Pith" description="What Pith collects when you send the form, why, and what you can ask us to do with it.">
  <main class="legal">
    <h1><span class="mask" style="--d:.15s"><span>Privacy<span class="pop dot" style="--d:.6s">.</span></span></span></h1>
    <div class="body rv" style="--d:.35s">
      <p class="lead">Short, because there isn't much to say. We collect what we need to reply to you, and nothing else.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Pith is a trading name of Liam Scott Digital Ltd, registered in England and Wales, company number 17243833. Registered office: 9 Greyfriars Road, Reading RG1 1NU. We're the data controller for anything you send us here. Questions go to <a class="u" href="mailto:liam@lsdagency.co.uk">liam@lsdagency.co.uk</a>.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send the form: the three things you chose, your work email, and your name if you gave it. Our host, Netlify, also records the submission with your IP address and browser type. We pass your message, email and name to HubSpot, which is where we keep track of conversations.</p>

      <h2>Why</h2>
      <p>To read what you sent and reply to it. That's our legitimate interest in answering an enquiry you chose to make. If we end up working together, the details become part of the client record.</p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts. We don't sell or share your details, and we won't add you to a mailing list because you sent a form.</p>

      <h2>Where it lives and for how long</h2>
      <p>Submissions are stored by Netlify and HubSpot, both established providers with their own safeguards for data held outside the UK. If we don't end up working together, we delete the enquiry within twelve months.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask to see what we hold, have it corrected or deleted, or object to us using it. Email <a class="u" href="mailto:liam@lsdagency.co.uk">liam@lsdagency.co.uk</a> and we'll sort it. If you're not happy with how we've handled it, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a class="u" href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

      <p class="date">Last updated 15 September 2026.</p>
      <p><a class="u back" href="/">Back to the page</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
  .legal { flex: 1; max-width: 62ch; padding: clamp(32px, 6vh, 72px) 0 clamp(40px, 8vh, 96px); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 72px); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .lead { font-size: clamp(18px, 1.5vw, 21px); line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .date { margin-top: 32px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mono60); }
  .back { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; }
</style>
